SUMMARY:The Atlanta Odyssey — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T160000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:d5c2db1db903c4c34094016fe3ec@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Books\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:‘The Atlanta Odyssey’ is Robert Barsky’s new illustrated
  epic poem. Inspired Homer’s Odyssey\, this work is being created to ref
 lect great epic quests from the past\, and inspire future journeys through
  Atlanta and Fulton County. The work highlights the many layers of Atlanta
 ’s history\, and brings the reader along for the ride by adding photos a
 nd soundscapes of graffiti\, artworks and landmarks recorded en route. Thi
 s project features the poet George\, of ‘Beltline Chronicles fame’\, w
 ho wanders around Atlanta and creates an epic story of his adventures alon
 g the way. Robert Barsky will join Susan Ker-Seymer at the Book//Zine\, Bu
 rnaway’s annual art book and zine fair at the Goat Farm. This event\nCat
 egory: Books\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-atlanta-
 odyssey/
LOCATION:Goat Farm\, 1200 Foster Street NW\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30318
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-atlanta-odyssey/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
