SUMMARY:Exhibit | Divine Afterlife: Burials and Religion in Ancient Egypt 
 — Providence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T150000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:9aa94c1152cdb3a6b6481387e7db@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\, Open to the Public\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:This exhibit of photographs by Brown alumnus and current Brown
  Medical student Akshay Amesur\, presented at the Joukowsky Institute of A
 rchaeology and the Ancient World at Brown University\, features a curated 
 collection of images exploring funerary and religious practices in ancient
  Egypt. Drawing on visual documentation of tombs\, temples\, and ritual sp
 aces\, the exhibit offers glimpses into how ancient Egyptians understood d
 eath\, the afterlife\, and the divine.\nCategory:  Open to the Public\nOri
 ginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/joukowsky-archaeology/event/341510
 -exhibit-divine-afterlife-burials-and-religion-in-anci
