BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibit | Scents of the Ancient Past (Curated by Erynn Bentley ’
 27) — Providence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T150000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:5932070ac1073407a32ddd6ae5f5@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\, Open to the Public\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The perfumes of the ancient world were not quite like those we
  use today. For starters\, unlike the alcohol-based brands we’re familia
 r with\, ancient perfume was oil based and composed of natural ingredients
 . Furthermore\, beyond just making the wearer smell good\, these often ela
 borate concoctions served a myriad of purposes: communing with the gods\, 
 showing off your status in life (and in death)\, and even healing—or per
 haps…bewitching—the body. Follow your nose on this olfactory journey\,
  from Ancient Egypt to Roman London and beyond\, and explore what scents t
 he past has to offer in this exhibit: Scents of the Ancient Past Curated b
 y Erynn Bentley (’26\, Ph.D. expected)\nCategory:  Open to the Public\nO
 riginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/joukowsky-archaeology/event/3415
 11-exhibit-scents-of-the-ancient-past-curated-by-erynn-b
LOCATION:Rhode Island Hall\, Rhode Island Hall
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/joukowsky-archaeology/event/341511-exhibit-sc
 ents-of-the-ancient-past-curated-by-erynn-b
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
