BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: La maison des bois: Episodes 4–7 — Berkeley/Sa
 n Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261024T140000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:d5c9276f52e92f9205ef9d289dfd@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Epic yet intimate\, sweeping yet personal\, La maison des bois
  stands as one of the greatest achievements in the history of television\,
  as well as legendary director Maurice Pialat’s magnum opus. Commissione
 d for Télévision Française in 1971\, this seven-episode\, nearly four-h
 undred-minute miniseries considers the impact of World War I on a simple F
 rench family living in the countryside. Applying a naturalistic focus to t
 heir subject\, Pialat and screenwriter René Wheeler capture both the hist
 orical scope of the conflict and the subtle ways that a small town’s quo
 tidian routines and rituals—church\, school\, tavern—are indelibly tou
 ched by it.\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.ed
 u/BAMPFA/event/328123-film-screening-la-maison-des-bois-episodes-47
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328123-film-screening-la-mais
 on-des-bois-episodes-47
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
