BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kim Ouellette “Emerald Tears” — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T180000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T210000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:d65f840b3a6ef05d5f48e7fdeb22@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Art + Design\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Marcia Wood Gallery is pleased to present “Emerald Tears”
 \, a solo exhibition of new paintings by Atlanta-based artist Kim Ouellett
 e. This is Ouellette’s third solo exhibition with the gallery. Her absor
 bing paintings are sought after for their lush color\, tactile surfaces\, 
 and polyphonic compositions. The title comes from a chance discovery: whil
 e working with a new emerald green paint\, Ouellette came across “Emeral
 d Tears”\, Dave Holland’s solo bass album. Its melancholy\, she says\,
  connects to the mood of the new paintings\, where the green returns like 
 a single voice moving through a space. Each work announces itself at once
 \, then slowly opens into a field of small discoveries. Kim Ouellette\nCat
 egory: Art + Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/kim-o
 uellette-emerald-tears/
LOCATION:Marcia Wood Gallery\, 764-D Miami Circle NE\, Atlanta\, GA\, 3032
 4
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/kim-ouellette-emerald-tears/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
