DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261025T190000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:6c48952c01d6e672bcfe30a1d415@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Exhibits\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:On display from Sep 9 - Dec 13\, 2026 | 11 am - 7 p.m. Bookend
 ed by the end of World War II in 1945 and the fall of the Berlin Wall in 1
 989\, the Cold War was a transformative period in global history\, marking
  both the end of the twentieth century and the waning of modernism. Though
  earlier historians defined the Cold War as the noncombative contest betwe
 en the capitalist United States and the communist Soviet Union\, recent in
 terventions by scholars\, artists\, and writers have stressed that this pe
 riod was also defined by the struggles for decolonization and national lib
 eration movements across Asia and globally. Undeniable to the history of t
 he Cold War is the crucial role that culture played \nCategory: Exhibits\n
 Original listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/csas/event/326757-bampfa-exh
 ibition-private-frontiers-media-legacies
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/csas/event/326757-bampfa-exhibition-privat
 e-frontiers-media-legacies
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
