DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:a80d23ddc81bbafef7c8e53db78c@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A coffee shop flirtation with Marcy (Rosanna Arquette) sends h
 apless office worker Paul (Griffin Dunne) downtown for a date in this zany
  Kafkaesque comedy set in the artists’ lofts\, dive bars\, diners\, club
 s\, and streets of a yet-to-be gentrified SoHo—a different kind of under
 world for Martin Scorsese. Cinematographer Michael Ballhaus\, in his first
  collaboration with the director\, effectively captures the sinister\, ali
 en quality of the city at night. Things go from weird to worse for Paul wi
 th each subsequent encounter—hilarious scenes with Catherine O’Hara an
 d Teri Garr—as he tries to extricate himself from cascading misfortune.
 \nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/ev
 ent/328126-film-screening-after-hours
