BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibition on View | Building Books with Dayanita Singh — Provid
 ence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261026T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:ade414963c886c7283da64ebfe16@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\, Open to the Public\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In her practice\, Dayanita Singh experiments with form through
  photography\, architecture\, and books to create exhibitions. Using these
  mediums\, Singh extends an invitation to audiences to question how books
 \, and book-making\, might transform a space into an exhibition. This show
  takes cues from Singh’s artist-led approach to exhibitions to explore t
 he relationship between “making” and “reading.” With Singh’s Boo
 k Building (2022) as a blueprint\, this exhibition analyzes book-making as
  an artistic practice\, material form\, and conceptual process. Works in t
 he exhibition span Singh’s career\, including Book Building (2022)\, Blu
 e Book (2009)\, File Room (2013)\, Museum of Chance (2014)\, and Sent a Le
 t\nCategory:  Open to the Public\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.e
 du/bai/event/338354-exhibition-on-view-building-books-with-dayanita-singh
LOCATION:Granoff Center for the Creative Arts\, Granoff Center for the Cre
 ative Arts
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/bai/event/338354-exhibition-on-view-building-
 books-with-dayanita-singh
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibit | Centering Philippine and Filipinx American Histories: Se
 lections from The Bancroft Library — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261026T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:c2b1af6795c9ec1138abe145494f@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Exhibits\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The Bancroft Library’s collections of materials relating to 
 the Philippines span nearly 500 years. Highlights in this exhibit include 
 a transcript of an Inquisitorial trial from 1646\, a prayer book written i
 n the Cebuano language\, and UC Berkeley Filipino student publications fro
 m 1905 to the present. The exhibit also features selections from the perso
 nal papers of acclaimed author Jessica Hagedorn\, including typewritten dr
 afts of her novels\, poetry\, song lyrics\, and a screenplay\, as well as 
 childhood drawings and writings. Open hours may vary. Please view the The 
 Bancroft Library hours page for the most up-to-date information.\nCategory
 : Exhibits\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/Library/event/28
 8815-centering-philippine-and-filipinx-american
LOCATION:The Bancroft Library (corridor)\, The Bancroft Library (corridor)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/Library/event/288815-centering-philippine-
 and-filipinx-american
