UID:5cb519f72b1f449237619453b1fe@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Asia’s seas have long served as arenas of commerce\, coopera
 tion\, contestation\, and conflict. Today\, the maritime expanse stretchin
 g from the Indian Ocean to the Arctic stands at the center of global geopo
 litics\, economic flows\, environmental pressures\, and strategic competit
 ion—military\, legal\, and otherwise. With these dynamics in mind\, this
  conference seeks to foster interdisciplinary dialogue on how maritime dom
 inance is conceptualized\, pursued\, and contested across Asian contexts. 
 Agenda Thursday\, October 29: 1:30PM: Opening Remarks Andrew Wilson\, U.S.
  Naval War College Bruce Dickson\, George Washington University 1:45-3:15P
 M: Panel I—Indian Ocean Darshana M. Baruah\, Shangri-La Dialogue S\nCate
 gory: Academic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/claiming-
 the-sea-asian-perspectives-on-maritime-dominance
LOCATION:1957 E Street NW\, 1957 E St NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/claiming-the-sea-asian-perspectives-on-
 maritime-dominance
