DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:6dc5f63aaf4357161fb8356d09dc@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Join the GW Department of American Studies for part one of our
  2026-27 Mergen-Palmer Distinguished Lecture Series featuring Prof. Justin
  Mann\, associate professor of English at Northwestern University\, and a 
 GW American Studies PhD alum. “Getting Lost in the Dark” analyzes two 
 texts\, Victor La Valle and Dietrich Smith’s graphic novel Destroyer and
  the Russo brothers' Captain America: The Winter Soldier \, to show how Bl
 ack speculative fictions reimagine the possibilities\, limits\, and potent
 ial ends of the American security state.\nCategory: Academic\nOriginal lis
 ting: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/2026-mergen-palmer-distinguished-lect
 ure-part-i-prof-justin-mann
