UID:13c7d0b09a4eb34cbf7ea88bcc67@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:Guns Without Borders: Illicit Arms Trafficking\, State Respons
 ibility\, and the Inter-American Human Rights System The event will focus 
 on the Inter-American Court of Human Rights’ recent Advisory Opinion OC-
 30/25\, an important development in the Inter-American human rights system
  addressing the relationship between firearms\, State obligations\, and th
 e protection of human rights. Rather than presenting the issue as a formal
  debate or from a single viewpoint\, the discussion will examine the legal
  questions\, practical tensions\, and competing considerations raised by O
 C-30/25 and by efforts to address gun violence that crosses national borde
 rs. The event will be livestreamed. Please register to r\nCategory: Lectur
 es & Speakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/panel-disc
 ussion-guns-without-borders
LOCATION:Law School\, 2000 H St NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/panel-discussion-guns-without-borders
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
