CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Art + Design\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:What does it mean to grow older in a queer body\, surrounded b
 y queer community? Join MODA’s Queer Figure Drawing Night with Ashanti H
 ampton for Queer Across Generations\, a special session celebrating queer 
 bodies across time. For this gathering\, we’ll welcome a queer elder as 
 our model and make space to consider the beauty\, complexity\, and possibi
 lity of aging. So many of us carry questions about what it means to grow o
 lder: Will I be allowed to age? What does it look like to grow older in my
  body and in my community? Through drawing\, we’ll honor aging as someth
 ing visible\, beautiful\, and possible\, and celebrate the bodies and stor
 ies that have helped make queer community what it is today. C\nCategory: A
 rt + Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/queer-figure-
 drawing-queer-across-generations/
