SUMMARY:Eric Gottesman’s NIGHT AND DAY — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261106T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261106T170000
DTSTAMP:20261025T162751Z
UID:c2d1273a0022cc079467b486bc19@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:For Freedoms presents artist and educator Eric Gottesman’s N
 IGHT AND DAY which centers on Ethiopian journalist and author Baalu Girma
 ’s controversial 1984 Amharic novel Oromay \, written under the Derg reg
 ime and banned shortly after its publication. Drawing on Gottesman’s dee
 p engagement with the novel\, NIGHT AND DAY considers how artists create\,
  communicate\, and sustain cultural memory within and against conditions o
 f censorship\, political repression\, and state violence. The exhibition e
 xtends beyond the gallery through a library of banned books\, a self-guide
 d workshop station that invites visitors to respond to censorship through 
 writing and drawing\, and a public conversation on how artist\nCategory: A
 rts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/eric-gotte
 smans-night-and-day
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/eric-gottesmans-night-and-day
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
